Arcade bar: loading a state doesn't restart the SH4's serial port timer.

SCIFSerialPort::deserialize restored the SCIF's two scheduler entries from the state (V43 and up)
and then called updateBaudRate(), which requests the transmit timer again from "now": the SH4's
clock at that point is still the one from before the load (the context and the scheduler base
come later in the state). Two machines loading the same state had that timer due at different
cycles, and saving right after loading gave different bytes. Now the baud rate is recomputed
without rescheduling when the state carried the timers.

diff --git a/core/hw/sh4/modules/serial.cpp b/core/hw/sh4/modules/serial.cpp
--- a/core/hw/sh4/modules/serial.cpp
+++ b/core/hw/sh4/modules/serial.cpp
@@ -441,6 +441,19 @@
 		transmitting = false;
 	}
 	SCIF_SCBRR2 &= 0xff;	// work around previous issues with dynarecs
+#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__
+	// Arcade bar (flycast/patches/0006): the state brought the serial timers back (V43 and up);
+	// rescheduling here restarted the transmit timer from "now" before the SH4's clock itself was
+	// restored (it comes later in the state), i.e. from the time of whatever ran before the load:
+	// two machines loading the same state then had that timer due at different cycles.
+	if (deser.version() >= Deserializer::V43)
+	{
+		frameSize = 1 + 8 - SCIF_SCSMR2.CHR + SCIF_SCSMR2.PE + 1 + SCIF_SCSMR2.STOP;
+		int bauds = SH4_MAIN_CLOCK / 4 / (SCIF_SCBRR2 + 1) / 32 / (1 << (SCIF_SCSMR2.CKS * 2));
+		cyclesPerBit = SH4_MAIN_CLOCK / bauds;
+		return;
+	}
+#endif
 	updateBaudRate();
 }
 
